<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pensacola</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pensacola is a port city on Pensacola Bay in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>. A short-lived Spanish colony was planted there in 1559, and a lasting Spanish settlement was founded in 1698. The city served as capital of British West Florida from 1763, was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-de-galvez">Bernardo de Gálvez</a> in 1781 and passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> with the rest of Florida in 1821.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pensacola.jpg" alt="Pensacola" width="320" height="542" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dom Price (Skyline Photo) Ebyabe (Photos of the Customhouse and Plaza Ferdinand Only), Thomas Baxter (Photo of library at UWF) … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Collage_of_images_from_around_Pensacola.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
